    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0329" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg223"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-09-20">September 20,
                                1906</date></hi>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 174.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a dispatch<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d201-f1"/> from the embassy at Tokyo, in regard to the open door in
                    Manchuria, in which special reference is made to the necessity for the
                    establishment of customs-houses in that region.</p>
                <p>You are requested to represent to the Russian Government the importance the
                    United States attaches to the early establishment of Chinese customs-houses on
                    the line of the Chinese Eastern Railway.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
